    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://cropontology.org/rdf/Measurement"/>
    <ns1:definition xml:lang="en">Fiber Spinning Consistency Index (SCI)  is an HVI measurement calculated value based on a regression equation. This equation takes into account all HVI properties and calculates one value to be used on each sample tested. The SCI is an index derived with data from a large number of cotton samples having a wide range in properties that is related to test data from yarn spun from each sample</ns1:definition>
  </ns2:Class>
